
    Plot the limaçon of Pascal
    
    The limaçon is a fourth-order curve defined by
    the parametric equations:
    
        x = (b + a cos t) cos t
        y = (b + a cos t) sin t
        
    The parameters a and b control the shape of the
    curve and whether it has a cusp or inner loop.
        
    References:
        http://mathworld.wolfram.com/Limacon.html
        https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lima%C3%A7on

A set decimal places to 25
A write numbers with decimal point

N100 2.0        . Parameter a
N101 1.0        . Parameter b
N110 0.25       . Global scale factor

N102 0.0        . t
